    16	---
    17	
    18	# ADR-073 — SemVer bump criteria for Sprint 32 closeout
    19	
    20	## Context
    21	
    22	PLAN-051 Phase 8 produces a final tag for the sprint. Three candidate
    23	versions are on the table:
    24	- **v1.9.0** — minor bump (no breaking changes)
    25	- **v1.10.0** — minor bump if accumulated changes warrant
    26	- **v2.0.0** — major bump (breaking change shipped)
    27	
    28	The decision drivers are mechanical (per SemVer 2.0.0 spec) but
    29	non-trivial because Phase 3 (audit_emit split — B1) may or may not
    30	ship a breaking refactor depending on approach selection in ADR-070
    31	+ Phase 3 execution.
    32	
    33	PLAN-051 §Phase 1 also intentionally already pushes `v1.9.0` GA tag at
    34	Phase 1 conclusion (independent of Phase 8) — so Phase 8 ALSO tags
    35	either v1.9.1 (patch on v1.9.0) or v1.10.0 / v2.0.0 (post-Phase-3+
    36	features merged).
    37	
    38	## Options considered
    39	
    40	### v1.9.0 — Phase 1 GA tag (committed)
    41	
    42	Per Phase 1 A3, this tag is signed + pushed BEFORE Phase 3 executes.
    43	It captures:
    44	- VERSION/npm align (3-minor-drift fix)
    45	- Grandfather.yaml warnings burn-down
    46	- All PLAN-050 closure (Sprint 31 done)
    47	- Pre-Sprint-32 governance state
    48	
    49	This is non-negotiable in Phase 1; ADR-073 only governs the **Phase 8
    50	closeout tag** decision.
    51	
    52	### Option A — v2.0.0 (if B1 ships breaking refactor)
    53	
    54	**Trigger:** Phase 3 ships `audit_emit_pkg/` canonical AND monolith
    55	`audit_emit.py` deleted (atomic swap successful).
    56	
    57	**Justification per SemVer:**
    58	- Public import path changes (`from _lib.audit_emit import X` may
    59	  remain a shim, OR may require `from _lib.audit_emit_pkg.core import X`
    60	  per chosen approach in ADR-070)
    61	- ADR-070 Approach 3 explicitly listed as "breaking change"
    62	- ADR-070 Approaches 1 & 2 may also break IF behavioral redaction or
    63	  any consumer-facing API changes
    64	
    65	### Option B — v1.10.0 (minor bump, no breaking)
    66	
    67	**Trigger:** Phase 3 ships `audit_emit_pkg/` AND ADR-070 Approach 1 or
    68	2 selected AND no public-API breakage AND backward-compat shim
    69	preserved.
    70	
    71	**Justification per SemVer:**
    72	- New features added (package layout, mutation budget 12→40, kill-
    73	  switch layers 4+6, conftest discovery, benchmark publication)
    74	- No existing consumer breaks
    75	- Minor bump appropriate
    76	
    77	### Option C — v1.9.1 (patch bump)
    78	
    79	**Trigger:** Phase 3 refused via ADR-070 + Phase 7 refused via ADR-072
    80	+ all other Phases ship without breaking changes.
    81	
    82	**Justification per SemVer:**
    83	- Only fixes (mutation budget, kill-switch wiring, benchmark publication)
    84	- No new public APIs
    85	- No breaking changes
    86	- Patch bump appropriate
    87	
    88	## Decision
    89	
    90	**Conditional decision:** version selected at Phase 8 closeout based on
    91	Phase 3 outcome:
    92	
    93	```
    94	IF B1 (audit_emit split) shipped:
    95	  IF chosen ADR-070 approach is breaking (Approach 3 OR explicit
    96	  breakage in 1/2):
    97	    → v2.0.0
    98	  ELSE:
    99	    → v1.10.0
   100	ELIF B1 refused (ADR-070 refused):
   101	  → v1.9.1
   102	```
   103	
   104	## Decision drivers
   105	
   106	1. **SemVer 2.0.0 strict compliance.** No marketing-driven SemVer
   107	   inflation; bump category derives from change category.
   108	
   109	2. **Adopter contract preservation.** v1.9.0 → v2.0.0 forces adopters
   110	   to read CHANGELOG before upgrade (npm/pip semver constraint
   111	   convention). Forcing this on a non-breaking change erodes adopter
   112	   trust.
   113	
   114	3. **Marketing alignment.** v2.0.0 is reserved for the milestone where
   115	   "audit cycle" (PLAN-052) ships if Owner pursues it post-Sprint-32.
   116	   This ADR does NOT pre-commit Phase 8 to v2.0.0.
   117	
   118	4. **Tag immutability.** Once pushed, npm registry semantics make tags
   119	   irreversible (yanking is a serious action). Decision rule must be
   120	   defensible at tag time.
   121	
   122	5. **Breaking-change definition** (per SemVer 2.0.0):
   123	   - Any public API import path change
   124	   - Any public API signature change (parameters, return type, raises)
   125	   - Any documented behavior change that consumers depend on
   126	   - Removal of any public symbol
   127	   - File-format change (audit-log JSONL schema, ADR frontmatter, etc.)
   128	
   129	   NOT breaking changes:
   130	   - Internal refactor preserved by shim
   131	   - Bug fix that aligns behavior to documentation
   132	   - Performance improvement (faster path, same semantics)
   133	   - Test additions
   134	   - New public API alongside existing one
   135	
   136	## Consequences
   137	
   138	### v1.9.1 path (Option C)
   139	- Lowest blast radius
   140	- Conservative messaging: "patch release, no new features"
