.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga-20260913-NOGO-r5/PROVENANCE-ga.md:1:# Proveniencia do re-pass do GA v1.4.0 (promocao da v1.4.0-rc.1) - PLAN-169 - 7 partes
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r12/verdict-rc1-6.txt:23:   **Concrete failure scenario:** the GC claims guaranteed coverage without starvation, but every sweep starts a fresh `scandir()` and stops at the 250 ms deadline. With a stable, sufficiently large prefix of unrelated or non-expired entries, every sweep stops before the same tail. Rotating the hash shard does not rotate the directory position, so expired markers in that tail can remain forever and accumulate.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r2/verdict-rc1-4.txt:9:- **P2 — [CONDITIONS-rc1.md:71](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc1.ceHJUv/wt/.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/CONDITIONS-rc1.md:71), [CONDITIONS-rc1.md:80](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-rc1.ceHJUv/wt/.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/CONDITIONS-rc1.md:80).** Conditions 15 and 16 are each used twice, making references in signed evidence ambiguous. **Minimal fix:** assign unique stable identifiers before signing.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-ga-20260913-NOGO-r2/verdict-ga-4.txt:25:   **Concrete failure scenario:** GA promotion changes the truth value of the unchanged rc.1 prose. The GA changelog still calls the artifact an rc/pre-release, says every P1 must be cured before GA, calls automatic migration a “pre-GA follow-up,” and explicitly says the seven-skill baseline migration “lands before GA.” It did not. A v1.3.0 copy-mode adopter trusting the GA changelog can upgrade normally and retain all seven VETO-bearing skills as `name-only`, exactly as condition 2 warns. The npm README likewise describes condition 84 as applying only “in this rc.” The envelope’s reinterpretation is accurate, but the shipped adopter-facing documents contradict it.  
