.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/payload-rc1-4.redacted.txt:2352:+| `session_memory_delta_observed` (v2.60) | `action`, `session_id` (str — threaded from the harness event, clamped ≤128, no silent default), `project` (str — `str(repo_root)`, clamped ≤256, the same field every event on this rail already carries), `outcome` (str — CLOSED enum `written` · `absent` · `index_only` · `start_unknown` · `dir_missing` · `not_writable` · `error` · `other`; off-enum COERCED to `other`, NEVER to `written` — an unparseable observation must never be laundered into a healthy-class value), `files_count` (int — clamped 0..99999; entries in the native memory dir), `modified_count` (int — clamped 0..99999; entries whose `st_mtime` falls inside THIS session's window — a WINDOW-scoped observation over the SHARED per-project dir: a CONCURRENT session's write inside the window counts (ADR-005 overlap is a supported case) and stat carries no author, so this is never an authorship claim), `index_modified` (bool — `MEMORY.md` specifically; non-bool coerced to `false`), `anchor_source` (str — CLOSED enum `chain` · `state_file` · `none`: which step of the session-start resolution answered — the HMAC chain's own `session_start` event via bounded scan (≤200 lines / ≤256 KiB / ≤100 ms; the OLDEST in-window match wins — a compact-restart re-emit for the same session id must not shrink the window — and a candidate is consumed only after its per-entry HMAC verifies against the previous line with the project key (verify-before-consume, ADR-160; `CEO_AUDIT_HMAC_DISABLE=1` waives the integrity claim; scope is PER-ENTRY — the candidate against the ADJACENT line's declared digest, the predecessor itself NOT re-verified: a same-UID log writer reads the 0600 key and forges whole chains anyway (CLAUDE.md §5 boundary), so whole-chain integrity stays `verify_chain`'s offline job, never this bounded reader's claim); the chain is the anchor, never a mutable side file — the ADR-160 §3 / A6 principle), `state_file` — RETIRED in this same ceremony (rail r5: the record file is rewritten via `os.replace` on every tool update, which allocates a NEW inode and resets even `st_birthtime` — no immutable artifact exists on that surface); the enum value stays registered for wire-compat and is NEVER produced. Resolution is therefore chain-or-`none`, with REAL predecessor resolution on the chain leg (legacy `hmac:null` prefix lines are traversed to the last SIGNED line, mirroring `verify_chain`; genesis applies only when the bounded window covers the whole file), or the terminal `none` = "I do not know": the hook never substitutes "since midnight" or process start, because a wrong window produces a false `written`, worse than absent), `event_schema`, `ts`, plus baseline `tokens_*`/`hmac`/`hmac_error`. PLAN-179 W2 US8 (wave-179-close ceremony; implements the signed spec `PLAN-179/staged-w24/SESSIONEND-NOTE.md`) — SessionEnd memory-delta observation: ONE emit per session from `.claude/hooks/SessionEnd.py::decide`, immediately BEFORE the `session_end` emit so a reader scanning backwards from `session_end` finds it adjacent. STAT-ONLY producer: counts `st_mtime >= session_start` over the native memory dir and NEVER opens a memory file for write — memory writing stays a model/Owner decision; the count is window activity over the project dir, not per-session authorship (rail r6 P2-a); this action makes the OMISSION visible (`outcome=absent` is the case the historical `memory_writable` bit could not express; structural namespace activity — rename/delete, detected via the directory mtime inside the window — BLOCKS the absence class and the index_only exclusivity, because the closed enum cannot express a structural delta and `error` is the honest refusal — rail r17). A NEW action deliberately, not extra fields on `session_end`: overloading would conflate "the hook ran" with "a delta was observed" and change the meaning of an event with a landed row (v2.7). Typed producer `emit_session_memory_delta_observed` routes through the dedicated deny-by-default `_SESSION_MEMORY_DELTA_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch with closed-enum VALUE re-coercion + TYPE-strict int clamps (bool is an int subclass, and a float would drop the ENTIRE event at the canonical-json layer — both coerce to the sentinel 0, never rounded, never echoed), NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire, by name — the scrub operates on field NAMES (non-allowlisted keys are dropped; identity fields `session_id`/`project` are type-checked and clamped, their VALUES being the emitter-wide baseline contract every action shares — the typed wrapper is the sole sanctioned producer and `test_no_paths_on_the_wire` pins what it sends): the memory file names/basenames (rail r22: names travel on NO channel at all — five rail rounds of directive-smuggling bypasses proved free-form basenames unsanitizable for an instruction-adjacent surface, so the operator line is COUNTS-ONLY and the sanitized `names` list remains an internal gate for any future render; this supersedes the earlier "names to the operator" split of the W2 AC, deviation declared), the file bodies or any excerpt, the resolved memory-dir absolute path and the `$HOME`-derived slug, the raw `session_start` source line, any environment value. Kill-switch `CEO_SESSION_MEMORY_DELTA` (unset = full; `quiet`/`1q` = event only, no operator line; `0`/`false`/`off`/`no` = nothing emitted — the `off` state needs NO gate-side waiver (rail r14, correcting the SESSIONEND-NOTE §104-108 model): the registered command remains a real hook, which the harness-config constant-emitter heuristic can never flag, and a substring allowlist entry would be inert for that purpose while opening an ADR-158 §2 bypass). Completeness residual (honest boundary, same as ADR-153 §H2): an ABSENT row is not evidence of an absent session — `CEO_EXTENDED_LIFECYCLE=0`, `disableAllHooks`, or a killed process all suppress it. Pre-registered DEATH criterion (SESSIONEND-NOTE.md §8): `outcome=absent` dominating a measurement window with no behaviour change means the rail is REMOVED, not kept as debt. NO ATLAS technique (governance/omission-visibility breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/payload-rc1-4.redacted.txt:2366:+| v2.59 | PLAN-179 W2 + W4 (staged-w24 pack, ADR-195 work-boundary persistence; Owner decision 2026-08-25 "3 actions — registra ledger_entry_rejected") — 3 NEW metadata-only actions. `ledger_checkpoint_recorded` + `ledger_checkpoint_skipped`: the ADVISORY work-boundary rail (`check_ledger_checkpoint.py`, PreToolUse/Bash) makes an OMITTED plan checkpoint visible at the one boundary this repo already has — a commit — instead of at session death, which S309 proved does not arrive. The two are separate actions so the measure-first window has a denominator. `ledger_entry_rejected`: the W4 ledger write-gate discard (`_lib/ledger_provenance.py`), which used to borrow `prompt_injection_detected` for `reason="scanner_hit"` and go breadcrumb-only for the other four reasons; that fallback rung is REMOVED with this registration, because filing an infrastructure discard as a DETECTION poisons the FPR series the window measures. All three route through dedicated deny-by-default `_scrub_*` branches (`_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_RECORDED_ALLOWLIST` / `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_SKIPPED_ALLOWLIST` / `_LEDGER_ENTRY_REJECTED_ALLOWLIST`), NONE is in `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`, and every integer field is TYPE-strict (`bool` rejected as an `int` subclass, `float` -> `0`, never rounded — S181 / ADR-055-AMEND-2). The commit message, the committed paths, the ledger content and the rejected entry body have no allowed field name at all. `_KNOWN_ACTIONS` 327 -> 330. ONE new typed emitter (`emit_ledger_entry_rejected`). HMAC chain shape + `verify_chain()` UNTOUCHED. | *(3 new per-action allowlists + closed enums `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_OUTCOMES` / `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_SKIP_REASONS` / `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_SCOPE_SOURCES` / `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_STATE_KINDS` / `_LEDGER_GATE_DECISIONS` / `_LEDGER_GATE_REASONS` / `_LEDGER_GATE_FAMILIES` + the TYPE-strict clamp `_ledger_int_field` in `audit_emit.py`; no new fields on `agent_spawn`)* |
.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w24/CLAUDE.md:97:- **Continuidade de compaction NÃO entrega (ADR-153 — fires-proof cumprido e NEGATIVO, S309 2026-08-16).** O autocompact real de 09:34Z disparou os dois hooks e entregou nada: `snapshot_outcome=scratchpad_unavailable`, `plan_id=unknown`, `snapshot_found=false`, `pointer_count=1`. Causa ESTRUTURAL: `resolve_plan_id` exige um `plan_transition` **da própria sessão**, e transição só ocorre em mudança de status — censo real: **2 eventos em 12.515 linhas**, ambos de outra sessão. A continuidade só funciona em sessões CURTAS, anti-correlacionada com o próprio caso de uso. O "residual risk #3" do ADR-153 é o caminho DOMINANTE, não a borda. Some-se: nada ESCREVE memória (`SessionEnd.py` só verifica gravabilidade), e o piso de thrashing deste repo é `T ≈ 107k` (`F+S` com o `F` medido) — **ACIMA do mínimo que a API permite** (`trigger.value=50000`), o que é pior que o `T ≈ 60k` que esta linha afirmava: com o piso real não existe limiar configurável que evite o thrashing. O `60k` derivava do `F = 50k` refutado; corrigido na S325 junto com os outros 9 sítios do mesmo folclore. **O `F` (piso re-pago) foi MEDIDO na S322 e é ~2× o que este arquivo publicava: 97.292 tokens na fronteira de uma compactação real** (= `TOTAL_IN` 112.638 − `postTokens` 15.346; decomposto em `cache_read` 68.980 + `cache_creation` 28.310), com controle independente cold-F na mesma sessão em 97.097 — delta de 0,20%. O folclore de ordem 44k que circulava no repo, e o `≈ 45–55k` que esta linha afirmava, estão **REFUTADOS** (o numeral exato do folclore está no relatório da medição, não aqui: um número aproximado em prosa de contrato não é vigiado por nenhuma regra de `verify-counts`, e o gate reprova por isso — corretamente). E `F` **não é constante**: série cold-F de n=41 (censura declarada) dá min 84.101 / mediana 98.636 / max 138.552, pstdev 16.148 — spread de 51,7% da média, então reportar só a média engana. Instrumento rastreado em `.claude/plans/PLAN-179/w0/gateboot_repay.py`. Cura do **PLAN-179** (`reviewed`; debate round-1 S312 = PROCEED com 9 emendas) **LANDADA neste corte para W0/W1/W1-b**: fallback por escopo de SESSÃO no snapshot (o gatilho deriva de PATHS, nunca de `resolve_plan_id`) e **Constraint Pinning** como constante de CÓDIGO em `_lib/pinned_constraints`, reinjetada por canal próprio (`SessionStart(matcher=compact)` + PostCompact) — ponteiro NÃO é restrição, e compactação apaga governança (medido em outro setup: 0% → 30–59% de violação). W2/W4 seguem staged (`PLAN-179/staged-w24/`); o flip de status do plano é decisão do Owner. Não tratar `additionalContext` em PostCompact como canal provado: a sonda (W0-1) está shipada, mas o veredito de canal ainda não rodou — exige uma compaction paga, operador/local.
.claude/plans/PLAN-179/staged-w24/CLAUDE.md:108:- **Night-run S328 (2026-08-25/26, conta alternativa, ~11 h autônomas; 7 commits não-canônicos landados a partir de `560dad0`): TRÊS pacotes de cerimônia esperam UM comando do Owner — `bash .claude/plans/PLAN-183/OWNER-S328-MORNING.sh` (ordem B → A → D; `README-MANHA.md`; pacote C do PLAN-185 NÃO iniciado por decisão do CEO: contexto do main chegou a 65 % antes de fechar A/B/D).** A = PLAN-183 W5-b fechamento (ADR-194 `ACCEPTED` + §7 ratificação da OQ-4 «Pista MISTA — braço C», retroativa a `6304f66`; discriminante de continuidade line-exact em `install.sh` — o `case` por substring casava `.github/CODEOWNERS.template` como prefixo, defeito de FORMA inerte; as duas frases da linha do ADR-194 acima entram no MESMO patch, atômicas com o flip). B = cura do gate hook-latency (Q5; desenho por 3 críticos anonimizados): a sonda de spawn é cega por construção; segunda chave RELATIVA `hook_p50 ≤ K_e × ref_p50` contra referência de EXECUÇÃO stdlib de 3 termos amostrada round-robin, 4 rótulos nomeados, **fase 1 advisory** (exit codes byte-idênticos; K só após ≥10 runs — `K_e = 1,25 × max R_e`, admissibilidade `K_e < (baseline_p50+150)/max ref_p50`, cap EXCLUSIVO) — o verde do `Validate` vem do rerun das 03:03, NÃO da fase 1; ADR-144 §S220 refutado (opts.model ROTEIA — W4.3). D = pack `staged-w24` montado e land-sim verde (3 ações, `_KNOWN_ACTIONS` 327→330, ADR-195, SPEC v2.59, CHANGELOG/docs pelo `verify-counts`), MANIFEST-based. **Medido na noite:** W4.1.0 live-fire (`PLAN-169/w4.1-probe-S328.md`) — sidecar fresco (3 s) mas `five_hour`=35 % no instante da recusa `session limit` ⇒ `used_pct` NÃO prova exaustão; zero Stop/rate na cadeia HMAC; 7 agentes caíram POR CHAMADA e foram RETOMADOS por `SendMessage` ao nome (transcript preservado — o mecanismo de continuidade que funcionou). `check-threat-model-freshness.py` ESCREVE `docs/threat-model.md` (accepted→stale, sempre) e derruba o P0 de qualquer SIGN — o MORNING reverte só esse flip. O rail codex desta versão NÃO emite `VERDICT:` — rodada limpa = ausência do bloco `Full review comments:`. Sobre o censo untracked do PLAN-185 o rail devolveu +16 achados da classe "forma não modelada ⇒ fail-open" (5 rodadas) — insumo da 4ª passada invertida. 13 OQs novas esperam o Owner (PLAN-183 5-11; PLAN-169 7-12). **Manhã de 26/08: B LANDADO (`4bd7def`) e A LANDADO (`3bc3638`), assinados pelo Owner — ADR-194 `ACCEPTED`, gate fase 1 vivo no `validate.yml`; D parou no SIGN (P1 fail-closed: o land de A mudou o `CLAUDE.md` depois de o pack ser montado) — cura por ITEM (re-derivar a cópia do pack do vivo novo, re-montar, commitar) e `OWNER-S328-MORNING.sh --from D`; procedimento na memória `project-s328-night-run-state`.**
