ved` routes through the dedicated deny-by-default `_SESSION_MEMORY_DELTA_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST` scrub branch with closed-enum VALUE re-coercion + TYPE-strict int clamps (bool is an int subclass, and a float would drop the ENTIRE event at the canonical-json layer — both coerce to the sentinel 0, never rounded, never echoed), NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire, by name — the scrub operates on field NAMES (non-allowlisted keys are dropped; identity fields `session_id`/`project` are type-checked and clamped, their VALUES being the emitter-wide baseline contract every action shares — the typed wrapper is the sole sanctioned producer and `test_no_paths_on_the_wire` pins what it sends): the memory file names/basenames (rail r22: names travel on NO channel at all — five rail rounds of directive-smuggling bypasses proved free-form basenames unsanitizable for an instruction-adjacent surface, so the operator line is COUNTS-ONLY and the sanitized `names` list remains an internal gate for any future render; this supersedes the earlier "names to the operator" split of the W2 AC, deviation declared), the file bodies or any excerpt, the resolved memory-dir absolute path and the `$HOME`-derived slug, the raw `session_start` source line, any environment value. Kill-switch `CEO_SESSION_MEMORY_DELTA` (unset = full; `quiet`/`1q` = event only, no operator line; `0`/`false`/`off`/`no` = nothing emitted — the `off` state needs NO gate-side waiver (rail r14, correcting the SESSIONEND-NOTE §104-108 model): the registered command remains a real hook, which the harness-config constant-emitter heuristic can never flag, and a substring allowlist entry would be inert for that purpose while opening an ADR-158 §2 bypass). Completeness residual (honest boundary, same as ADR-153 §H2): an ABSENT row is not evidence of an absent session — `CEO_EXTENDED_LIFECYCLE=0`, `disableAllHooks`, or a killed process all suppress it. Pre-registered DEATH criterion (SESSIONEND-NOTE.md §8): `outcome=a