.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/diff-rc1-4.patch:1014:+| v2.59 | PLAN-179 W2 + W4 (staged-w24 pack, ADR-195 work-boundary persistence; Owner decision 2026-08-25 "3 actions — registra ledger_entry_rejected") — 3 NEW metadata-only actions. `ledger_checkpoint_recorded` + `ledger_checkpoint_skipped`: the ADVISORY work-boundary rail (`check_ledger_checkpoint.py`, PreToolUse/Bash) makes an OMITTED plan checkpoint visible at the one boundary this repo already has — a commit — instead of at session death, which S309 proved does not arrive. The two are separate actions so the measure-first window has a denominator. `ledger_entry_rejected`: the W4 ledger write-gate discard (`_lib/ledger_provenance.py`), which used to borrow `prompt_injection_detected` for `reason="scanner_hit"` and go breadcrumb-only for the other four reasons; that fallback rung is REMOVED with this registration, because filing an infrastructure discard as a DETECTION poisons the FPR series the window measures. All three route through dedicated deny-by-default `_scrub_*` branches (`_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_RECORDED_ALLOWLIST` / `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_SKIPPED_ALLOWLIST` / `_LEDGER_ENTRY_REJECTED_ALLOWLIST`), NONE is in `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`, and every integer field is TYPE-strict (`bool` rejected as an `int` subclass, `float` -> `0`, never rounded — S181 / ADR-055-AMEND-2). The commit message, the committed paths, the ledger content and the rejected entry body have no allowed field name at all. `_KNOWN_ACTIONS` 327 -> 330. ONE new typed emitter (`emit_ledger_entry_rejected`). HMAC chain shape + `verify_chain()` UNTOUCHED. | *(3 new per-action allowlists + closed enums `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_OUTCOMES` / `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_SKIP_REASONS` / `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_SCOPE_SOURCES` / `_LEDGER_CHECKPOINT_STATE_KINDS` / `_LEDGER_GATE_DECISIONS` / `_LEDGER_GATE_REASONS` / `_LEDGER_GATE_FAMILIES` + the TYPE-strict clamp `_ledger_int_field` in `audit_emit.py`; no new fields on `agent_spawn`)* |
