.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r8/verdict-rc1-5.txt:23:   Concrete failure: v1.4 introduces `$STATE_ROOT/scratchpad-session`, but creation and `sqlite3.connect()` follow directory and leaf symlinks. Its GC likewise accepts a symlinked store directory, scans the external directory, and unlinks old files named `session-<id>.sqlite{-wal,-shm}`. A path unused by v1.3 can therefore already be an adopter symlink or namespace; the first unresolved-plan PreCompact writes through it, and GC can delete matching external files. Condition 28 covers `<repo>/.claude/state`, not this native `$HOME`/`CEO_STATE_ROOT` store.
.claude/plans/PLAN-179/rail-round-11/VERDICT.txt:12:  If two store handles were opened before GC, GC can unlink the database and the first handle can recreate the path before the second obtains `FileLock`. The second handle then sees that the path exists and skips reopening, although its connection still targets the unlinked inode, so subsequent commits silently disappear. Detect path replacement as well as absence, or establish the connection while holding the lock.
