.claude/plans/PLAN-179/rail-round-10/VERDICT.txt:6:  When another process begins opening an aged session store, it opens the SQLite database before acquiring the external `FileLock`; this GC can acquire that lock first and unlink the database, WAL, and SHM underneath the already-open connection. The writer can then fail or commit into an unlinked database, losing the continuity snapshot, so deletion must be coordinated with database opening rather than only the later read/write lock.
