   286	default `--on-conflict=refuse` (backup kept; ownership and the rewritten
   287	manifest pass to the framework) — signed condition of rc.1. Before
   288	upgrading, run this validator from the target root (python3, standard
   289	library only). It requires a regular file that is not a symlink; every line
   290	in the loader's grammar (HASH record = 64 lowercase hex, two spaces, relpath;
   291	LINK record = `LINK`, two spaces, relpath, two spaces, target); only
   292	CANONICAL spellings (`./x`, `a//b`, `a/./b`, a trailing slash and `..` are
   293	refused — the loader keeps the original spelling and the lookup demands
   294	exact text, so an alias becomes FALLBACK); no control byte anywhere; at
   295	least one record (a zero-byte manifest is "no manifest" to the loader, and
   296	the upgrade then takes the legacy delete-and-recopy path); no relpath
   297	recorded twice, textually or by identity (two spellings of one inode). It
   298	must print nothing and exit 0:
   299	
   300	```bash
   301	python3 - <<'PY'
   302	import os, re, sys
   303	f = ".claude/.install-manifest.sha256"
   304	if os.path.islink(f) or not os.path.isfile(f):
   305	    print("BAD manifest: missing, a symlink, or not a regular file"); sys.exit(1)
   306	bad = n = 0; seen = {}; ident = {}; ctl = re.compile(r"[\x00-\x1f\x7f]")
   307	for i, line in enumerate(open(f, "rb").read().decode("utf-8", "replace").split("\n"), 1):
   308	    if line == "" or line.startswith("#"):
   309	        continue
   310	    if line.startswith("LINK  "):
   311	        parts = line[6:].split("  ", 1); rel = parts[0]
   312	        ok = len(parts) == 2 and parts[1] != "" and not ctl.search(parts[1])
   313	    else:
   314	        parts = line.split("  ", 1); rel = parts[1] if len(parts) == 2 else ""
   315	        ok = len(parts) == 2 and re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{64}", parts[0]) is not None and "  " not in rel
   316	    comps = rel.split("/")
   317	    ok = ok and rel != "" and not rel.startswith("/") and not ctl.search(rel) \
   318	        and os.path.normpath(rel) == rel and "" not in comps and "." not in comps and ".." not in comps
   319	    if not ok:
   320	        print("BAD line %d" % i); bad += 1; continue
   321	    n += 1
   322	    if rel in seen:
   323	        print("DUP " + rel); bad += 1
   324	    seen[rel] = i
   325	    try:
   326	        st = os.lstat(rel); ident.setdefault((st.st_dev, st.st_ino), []).append(rel)
   327	    except OSError:
   328	        pass
   329	for rels in ident.values():
   330	    if len(rels) > 1:
   331	        print("ALIAS " + " = ".join(sorted(rels))); bad += 1
   332	if n == 0:
   333	    print("BAD manifest: no record"); bad += 1
   334	sys.exit(1 if bad else 0)
   335	PY
   336	```
