P1 — FILE:LINE: [check_postcompact_reinject.py:379](<WT>/.claude/hooks/check_postcompact_reinject.py:379), [check_postcompact_reinject.py:389](<WT>/.claude/hooks/check_postcompact_reinject.py:389), [CONDITIONS-rc1.md:935](<WT>/.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/CONDITIONS-rc1.md:935). PreCompact and PostCompact independently resolve the plan. If PreCompact sees no transition yet and writes the session store, then a delayed async-spool drain exposes an exact `PLAN-123` before PostCompact, PostCompact reads only the empty plan store and returns no snapshot; it never falls back to the session store. A branch probe produced `result=None session_fallback_calls=0`. This falsifies condition 70’s claim that exact `PLAN-NNN` IDs guarantee continuity. Minimal fix: on a plan-store miss, read the trusted hook-input session store and accept a `scope_kind=session` snapshot; add an unknown→`PLAN-123` visibility-change round-trip test.

P1 — FILE:LINE: [state_store.py:126](<WT>/.claude/hooks/_lib/state_store.py:126), [test_isolation.py:197](<WT>/.claude/hooks/_lib/test_isolation.py:197), [test_isolation.py:383](<WT>/.claude/hooks/_lib/test_isolation.py:383). The isolation layer neutralizes `CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR_NATIVE` and redirects audit carriers, but omits `CEO_STATE_ROOT`, which has absolute precedence in `state_store`. Running pytest with an ambient `CEO_STATE_ROOT` therefore lets compaction tests create or overwrite real scratchpad SQLite state outside the isolated tree. A resolver probe with isolated `HOME`, project and audit paths still returned `/operator/live-state`. This violates the repository’s test-environment isolation rule and is absent from the envelope. Minimal fix: redirect, clear and validate `CEO_STATE_ROOT` in the collection window, session fixture, `TestEnvContext`, and subprocess environment; add an external-canary test.

P2 — FILE:LINE: [check_postcompact_reinject.py:677](<WT>/.claude/hooks/check_postcompact_reinject.py:677), [audit_emit.py:8890](<WT>/.claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:8890), [CONDITIONS-rc1.md:603](<WT>/.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/CONDITIONS-rc1.md:603). The emitter docstring still says `constraint_count` will be dropped “until” it is allowlisted, while the shipped allowlist already contains it. Condition 38 expressly claims this stale clause was cured, so the proposed signed text is factually wrong. Minimal fix: update the canonical docstring or amend condition 38 to declare it unresolved.

P2 — FILE:LINE: [mcp-smoke.yml:314](<WT>/.github/workflows/mcp-smoke.yml:314), [mcp-smoke.yml:323](<WT>/.github/workflows/mcp-smoke.yml:323). The workflow claims to assert an intact HMAC chain, but only counts parseable JSON and silently ignores malformed records; broken `prev`/HMAC values therefore pass. Minimal fix: invoke the real chain verifier, or rename and document the step as JSON-readability-only.

