Concrete failure scenario: a v1.3.0 adopter follows condition 27 exactly and copies `state/scratchpad/`, `skill_proposals/`, `skill_index/` and `session_graph/`. `/resume PLAN-123` ignores all those stores: it searches `<runtime-root>/session-graphs/` and otherwise rebuilds from audit-log, git and plan markdown. Because the legacy audit log is intentionally left behind, the rebuilt graph silently loses the pre-upgrade session/event history. Likewise, conditions 19 and 70 falsely say `/resume` can read a missed PostCompact snapshot; `/resume` never reads `compaction_continuity` or any SQLite state store.  
Minimal fix: remove the `/resume` claims from conditions 19/27/70 and document the actual loss, or implement and test dual-read/migration for `session-graphs/` plus legacy audit history. Amend the frozen envelope and rerun the re-pass.

